<title>SWEDEN: ERICSSON WINS FIVE-YEAR NEW ZEALAND ORDER.</title>
<headline>ERICSSON WINS FIVE-YEAR NEW ZEALAND ORDER.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group Ericsson said on Wednesday it signed a five-year mobile telephone network contract with Telecom New Zealand worth between 1.58 billion and 2.76 billion crowns.</p>
<p>&quot;Ericsson and Telecom New Zealand have signed a five-year contract for supply and support of Telecom's mobile telephone network of the D-AMPS standard (IS-136 TDMA),&quot; Ericsson said in a statement.</p>
<p>The contract will ensure New Zealand Telecom's possibilities to operate a network with increased coverage and PCS services, it said.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
